# Tool set for recon-toolkit.
# This file is documentation, not a manifest the build reads. Keep it in sync
# with the Dockerfile. The ProjectDiscovery tools are installed as a full stack
# via pdtm (ProjectDiscovery Tool Manager), so the PD list below is indicative,
# not exhaustive — pdtm installs the whole suite.

## Network / port
nmap                 # port + service/version scanning, NSE scripts
masscan              # fast wide-range port sweeps
naabu                # fast port scanning (ProjectDiscovery)
netcat-traditional   # manual connections / banner grabbing

## DNS
dnsutils             # dig, host, nslookup
dnsx                 # fast DNS resolution + record queries (ProjectDiscovery)
whois                # registration / ownership lookups

## Asset discovery
subfinder            # passive subdomain enumeration (ProjectDiscovery)
amass                # passive subdomain enumeration (OWASP)
waybackurls          # historical URLs from the Wayback Machine (tomnomnom)
gau                  # historical URLs from multiple sources (lc/gau)

## Web
httpx                # live-host probing + fingerprinting (ProjectDiscovery)
katana                # crawling / endpoint discovery (ProjectDiscovery)
whatweb              # technology fingerprinting
wappalyzer           # technology fingerprinting (tomnomnom CLI)
wafw00f              # WAF detection
gobuster             # content/directory discovery
feroxbuster          # recursive content discovery
ffuf                 # web fuzzing
gowitness            # web screenshots (needs chromium)

## OSINT
theharvester         # emails, hosts, subdomains from public sources

## Vulnerability
nuclei               # template-based scanning (ProjectDiscovery)
dalfox               # XSS scanning
sqlmap               # SQL injection testing

## Secrets
trufflehog           # secret scanning
gitleaks             # secret scanning (git-aware)

## TLS
sslscan              # protocols / cipher suites / cert details
tlsx                 # TLS data collection at scale (ProjectDiscovery)
testssl.sh           # thorough TLS assessment (pinned git checkout)

## ProjectDiscovery (other, via pdtm)
# uncover, asnmap, cdncheck, mapcidr, tlsx, notify, interactsh-client, and more.
# Run `pdtm -list` inside the container to see everything installed.

## Utility
curl wget jq ripgrep tmux vim less openssl git python3 chromium
